# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in the repository and checked out LF. Without
# this file the working tree's line endings depend on each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting: on a Windows clone with autocrlf unset, 53 files
# present as modified when nothing in them has changed, and no diff in the
# repository is readable. What the working tree holds is git's business; the
# committed content is LF and stays LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Exceptions. Nothing below may be normalised. ---

# Deliberate attack-string test data: this file carries a literal NUL byte at
# offset 1914, inside the array of URL schemes safeExternalHref must reject
# ("\x00javascript:alert(1)"). Git already auto-detects it as binary; saying
# so explicitly means no future normalisation pass can rewrite the NUL and
# silently stop the security test from testing the thing it is named after.
src/lib/externalUrl.test.ts -text

# Images.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary

# SQLite, should one ever land on a tracked path. .data/ is gitignored today.
*.db binary
